          "text": "The finiteness check should respect `lenient` mode. It should also run before `writeDeferredName()` so an invalid value does not partially modify the output or writer state.\n\n```java\n/**\n * Encodes {@code value}.\n *\n * @param value a finite value unless this writer is lenient\n * @return this writer\n */\npublic JsonWriter value(double value) throws IOException {\n  if (!lenient && (Double.isNaN(value) || Double.isInfinite(value))) {\n    throw new IllegalArgumentException(\n        \"Numeric values must be finite, but was \" + value);\n  }\n  writeDeferredName();\n  beforeValue();\n  out.append(Double.toString(value));\n  return this;\n}\n```"
